<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Shifu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th–14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Shifu was a Chinese playwright of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a>, author of The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romance-of-the-western-chamber">Romance of the Western Chamber</a>, a long <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaju">zaju</a> drama of love between the scholar Zhang Sheng and Cui Yingying. Based on a Tang story, the play was one of the most popular works of Chinese literature for centuries and was often criticised by moralists for its celebration of romantic love.</p></div>
